{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966808,"nonce":"mpJPNT79W2RhHHD3xK2jHPymiPI=","title":"web.rs runner never called invalidate_render_cache_tagged anywhere — composite-layer +","message":"On web (wasm), node_editor_demo's SVG icons rendered at correct positions on first paint, then drifted to STALE positions after:\n- Opening / closing an overlay (subgraph expand, context menu, popover)\n- Zooming the canvas via scroll wheel\n- Resizing the window\n\nIcons appeared at canvas-content coords baked at the moment a previous frame's overlay rebuild had run, ignoring subsequent viewport changes. Desktop was unaffected.\n\n\n`crates/blinc_app/src/web.rs` had ZERO calls to `invalidate_render_cache_tagged(...)`. `crates/blinc_app/src/windowed.rs` (desktop) calls it eleven times, tagged with `\"window_resized\"`, `\"state_changed\"`, `\"had_scroll\"`, `\"pointer_event_with_subscribers\"`, etc. The cache holds:\n- `motion_subtree_textures` baked by `render_subtree_to_layer_texture`\n- `css_composited_textures` from CSS-animated subtrees\n- `cached_motion_subtree_text_prims` / `cached_motion_subtree_svgs`\n\nThese survive every render call until something explicitly drops them. The slow walker on canvas-bearing pages re-emits primitives every frame, but the composite blits run AFTER the slow walker and overlay the stale textures on top of the fresh draws — exactly what the user saw.\n\n\nMirror the desktop runner's invalidation lifecycle in `web.rs`:\n\n- **wheel-drain (Phase 0b)** → `invalidate_render_cache_tagged(\"had_scroll\")` whenever a non-zero wheel delta is dispatched. Scroll updates the canvas-kit's pan/zoom matrix; cached textures baked under the old matrix have to drop.\n- **subtree-rebuild applied (Phase 2)** → `invalidate_render_cache_tagged(\"subtree_rebuild_applied\")` whenever `tree.process_pending_subtree_rebuilds()` returns true. Overlay open / close queues a rebuild; the textures keyed against the old element ids must go.\n- **animation-driven subtree rebuild (Phase 4)** → `invalidate_render_cache_tagged(\"animation_subtree_rebuild_applied\")` for the same reason.\n- **handle_resize** → `invalidate_render_cache_tagged(\"window_resized\")` so the post-resize frame re-rasterises every texture at the new extent.\n\n\nWhenever a new lifecycle event lands in the web runner that mutates element ids / coords / viewport — pointer events that reach subscribers, focus changes that trigger state styles, scroll-physics tick that updates offsets — add a matching `invalidate_render_cache_tagged(...)` call so the cache stays coherent. The desktop runner's `grep -n invalidate_render_cache_tagged windowed.rs` is the canonical list.\n\nLong-term: route web through `try_render_with_compositor` (currently desktop-only via `render_tree_with_motion_opt(Some(\u0026texture), try_fast_paint=true)`) so the compositor's own invalidation invariants apply. The web runner calls the wrapper `render_tree_with_motion(...)` which hard-codes `target_texture = None`, skipping the compositor entry path entirely.\n\n\n- [[gotcha-path-overlay-msaa-only-dispatch]] — sibling web-only bug from the same session (paths never dispatched on 1×-sample targets).\n- [[gotcha-web-right-click-swallowed]] — sibling web-only input bug from the same session (right-click swallowed without a focused editable).\n- `gotcha_p4_3_motion_subtree_bake_clip` — desktop motion-subtree bake fix; the cache existed correctly, the invalidation was missing on web.","files":null}]}